# Association for Psychological Science (APS)

> The Association for Psychological Science (APS) is a nonprofit membership organization founded in 1988, dedicated to the advancement of scientific psychology and its representation at the national and international level. APS publishes six peer-reviewed journals and the Observer magazine, hosts an annual convention, and advocates for behavioral and brain science. Headquartered in Washington, DC. This site hosts a full-text-indexed archive of 11,067 journal article records and the searchable programs of 14 APS conventions.

